# Notifications

A `claude-notifier` command is available in the sandbox. Use it for sparse, asynchronous notification of meaningful events.

## When to notify

| Event | Category |
| --- | --- |
| Build or test succeeds | `success` |
| Build or test fails | `error` |
| Three or more repeated failures | `frustration` |
| Important warning | `warning` |
| Requested task is complete | `task_complete` |
| User input is required | `attention` |
| A search found its target | `target` |
| A long task reaches a milestone | `encouragement` |
| A light sarcastic cue fits | `sarcasm` |

Run notifications in the background so they never delay work:

```bash
claude-notifier error &
```

Do not notify for routine tool calls, every commit, or every intermediate step. Notify no more than once per logical event.
